<https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2021/16/eng@/~part_XII__cl_78__subsec_2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://docs.oasis-open.org/legaldocml/ns/akn/3.0#subsection> <https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2021/16/eng@> .
<https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2021/16/eng@/~part_XII__cl_78__subsec_2> <https://schema.org/text> "Any interested person of any goods identified by homonymous geographical indication may, where no practical conditions in respect of the homonymous geographical indication have been imposed by the Registrar under section 11, apply to the Court for a declaration of the practical conditions under which the homonymous geographical indications are to be differentiated from each other, taking into account the need to ensure equitable treatment of the interested parties concerned and that the public are not misled."@en <https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2021/16/eng@> .
